{"name":"Dried Chervil","hex":"#b5bda3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dried","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without water or moisture, said of something that has previously been wet or moist; resulting from the process of drying.","Usually of foods: cured, preserved by drying."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of dry"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dried"},{"term":"chervil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A leafy herb, Anthriscus cerefolium, resembling parsley.","Leaves from the plant, used as an herb in cooking, which have a mild flavor of anise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chervil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Drying","blocks":[{"text":"Drying is a mass transfer process consisting of the removal of water or another solvent by evaporation from a solid, semi-solid or liquid. This process is often used as a final production step before selling or packaging products. To be considered \"dried\", the final product must be solid, in the form of a continuous sheet, long pieces, particles or powder. A source of heat and an agent to remove the vapor produced by the process are often involved. In bioproducts like food, grains, and pharmaceuticals like vaccines, the solvent to be removed is almost invariably water. Desiccation may be synonymous with drying or considered an extreme form of drying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Raumluft_waeschetrockner.jpg/330px-Raumluft_waeschetrockner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drying"},{"title":"Chervil","blocks":[{"text":"Chervil, sometimes called French parsley or garden chervil, is a delicate annual herb related to parsley. It was formerly called myrhis due to its volatile oil with an aroma similar to the resinous substance myrrh. It is commonly used to season mild-flavoured dishes and is a constituent of the French herb mixture fines herbes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Illustration_Anthriscus_cerefolium0.jpg/330px-Illustration_Anthriscus_cerefolium0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chervil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg/500px-Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg/1280px-Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg/500px-Stockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Drying of fish in Lofoten in the production of stockfish","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStockfish_in_Lofoten.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg/500px-Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg/960px-Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg/500px-Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFarmer's_Market_-_Chervil_(3497853296).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG/330px-Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG/330px-Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGraine_de_cerfeuil.JPG"}],"sounds":{"dried":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/En-us-dried.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/1a/En-us-dried.ogg/En-us-dried.ogg.mp3"}],"chervil":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-chervil.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-chervil.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-chervil.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-chervil.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-chervil.wav.ogg"}]}}}